flowchart TD
    AUTH[Validated current BootstrapAuthorityState and feature ID] --> HSCAN[ScanFeatureLogRunInventoryAction<br/>before any fresh current-run policy or binding is constructed;<br/>bounded no-follow inventory of all declared prior run/binding/stream header groups]
    HFINAL -- Valid --> FRAGMENT[Authority-owned CompiledFeatureLoggingPolicyFragment<br/>and its recorded config version; historical startup never reads changed root config]
    FRAGMENT --> LEVEL[CanonicalizeLogLevelAction<br/>FATAL stays fatal, CRITICAL aliases fatal, WARN aliases warning; case-normalize closed enum]
    LEVEL --> RANK[Bind severity rank<br/>fatal 60, error 50, warning 40, info 30, debug 20, trace 10]
    FRAGMENT --> PID[BuildFeatureLogPolicyIdAction<br/>exact feature, bootstrap-state, config-version and feature_logging slot tuple]
    PID --> POLICY[BuildFeatureLogPolicyAction then ValidateFeatureLogPolicyAction]
    DEFS[Closed PoC event-definition registry<br/>exact F0002 event to level, template, fields and sensitivity] --> POLICY
    DELIMITEDSCHEMA[Compiler-locked feature-log/v2 pipe-delimited constants<br/>38-column event and 30-column scalar prompt schemas;<br/>never supplied by config or generated dynamically] --> POLICY
    RANK --> POLICY
    FRAGMENT --> POLICY
    POLICY --> PBIND[Bind policy to fixed event and prompt collection artifact IDs]
    ROOTCFG[Fresh root logging config fragment] -. input only to identity-free bootstrap candidate compilation;<br/>never mixed with a historical current authority .-> BOOTCAND[BootstrapOperationalCandidate in diagram 08]

    CAP[Committed ActiveFeatureDirectoryCapability] --> BID[BuildFeatureLogBindingIdAction]
    ART[Validated WorkflowArtifactRegistry<br/>fixed featureDir/logs event and prompt collection IDs] --> BID
    RUN[Trusted feature ID, run ID and process metadata] --> BID
    PBIND --> BID
    BID --> BIND[ResolveFeatureLogBindingAction]
    CAP --> BIND
    BIND --> BVALID[ValidateFeatureLogBindingAction<br/>exact policy/binding tuple, contained append-only owner-only paths,<br/>regular files and no-follow ancestors]
    CAP --> HSCAN
    ART --> HSCAN
    RUN --> HSCAN
    BVALID --> SID[AssignFeatureLogSinkStateIdAction for the fresh current run]
    HSCAN --> HVALID{ValidateHistoricalFeatureLogRunInventoryAction<br/>exclude the fresh current run ID, validate bootstrap lineage and order every prior group}
    HVALID -- Invalid unknown corrupt or aliased group --> FAULT
    HVALID -- Valid --> HNEXT{Next prior-run binding/stream group}
    HNEXT -- Yes --> HAUTH[ResolveHistoricalFeatureLogAuthorityAction<br/>load the exact reachable historical bootstrap authority and persisted logging fragment]
    HAUTH --> HPOLICY[BuildHistoricalFeatureLogPolicyAction, recompute its tuple with<br/>BuildFeatureLogPolicyIdAction, then ValidateFeatureLogPolicyAction;<br/>never consult the current root config]
    HPOLICY --> HBIND[BuildFeatureLogBindingIdAction, ResolveFeatureLogBindingAction and<br/>ValidateFeatureLogBindingAction for the exact old run/binding group]
    HBIND --> HACQUIRE[AcquireFeatureLogStreamLockAction for the prior<br/>featureId, oldRunId and stream tuple under its historical binding]
    HACQUIRE -- Contention or acquisition failure --> FAULT
    HACQUIRE -- Raw observation --> HLOCK{ValidateFeatureLogStreamLockAction}
    HLOCK -- Invalid --> HREJECT[ReleaseRejectedFeatureLogStreamLockObservationAction]
    HREJECT --> FAULT
    HLOCK -- Valid --> HINSPECT[InspectFeatureLogStreamAction under the ordinary<br/>single historical-binding capability]
    HINSPECT -- existing-active-tail --> HRECOVER[RecoverFeatureLogTailAction<br/>validate pipe-delimited heading/control/data rows and truncate only<br/>an incomplete final event or prompt row]
    HRECOVER --> HCLOSE[CloseRecoveredHistoricalFeatureLogStreamAction<br/>fsync one crash-finalization trailer and create no successor segment]
    HINSPECT -- existing-closed-only --> HCLOSED[ValidateAlreadyClosedHistoricalFeatureLogStreamAction<br/>reconstruct finalization evidence without rewriting bytes]
    HINSPECT -- Missing or corrupt --> HFAILREL
    HCLOSE --> HRELEASE[ReleaseFeatureLogStreamLockAction<br/>release the ordinary prior-run capability with its terminal evidence]
    HCLOSED --> HRELEASE
    HRECOVER -- Failure --> HFAILREL[ReleaseFeatureLogStreamLockAction<br/>release the exact held historical capability with an error outcome]
    HCLOSE -- Failure --> HFAILREL
    HCLOSED -- Failure --> HFAILREL
    HFAILREL --> FAULT
    HRELEASE -- Released --> HCOLLECT[Collect the exact group identity, its typed close-or-already-closed<br/>finalization evidence and the matching successful release evidence]
    HCOLLECT --> HNEXT
    HRELEASE -- Failure --> FAULT
    HNEXT -- Complete --> HFINAL{ValidateHistoricalFeatureLogRunFinalizationAction<br/>consume the complete ordered inventory plus exactly one typed finalization disposition<br/>and successful release evidence for every prior group}
    HFINAL -- Invalid --> FAULT
    SID --> SNEXT{Next enabled stream without a startup lock}
    SNEXT -- Yes --> SACQUIRE[AcquireFeatureLogStreamLockAction<br/>one exact featureId, runId and stream tuple]
    SACQUIRE -- Contention or acquisition failure --> SFAILREL
    SACQUIRE -- Raw observation --> SLOCK{ValidateFeatureLogStreamLockAction<br/>exact owner, binding, adapter and runner lock-table uniqueness}
    SLOCK -- Invalid --> SREJECT[ReleaseRejectedFeatureLogStreamLockObservationAction<br/>terminalize the rejected raw acquired-lock observation and return typed release evidence]
    SREJECT --> SFAILREL
    SLOCK -- Valid --> SHOLD[Retain the opaque runner-held capability only in the lock table;<br/>never put its token in an envelope, state, telemetry or log]
    SHOLD --> SNEXT
    SNEXT -- Complete validated lock set held --> INSPECT[Run InspectFeatureLogStreamAction once per enabled stream<br/>with its exact matching held capability]
    INSPECT --> EXISTS{Complete startup inspection set}
    EXISTS -- No stream has a segment --> SEGID[AssignFeatureLogSegmentIdAction for the next enabled stream's ordinal one]
    SEGID --> CREATE[CreateInitialFeatureLogSegmentAction<br/>exclusive-create owner-only .log segment;<br/>exact pipe-delimited heading first, durable segment_header control row second]
    CREATE --> ISTREAM[BuildInitialFeatureLogStreamStateAction<br/>next sequence one and no durable event sequence]
    CREATE --> IRECORD[BuildInitialFeatureLogSegmentRecordAction<br/>active ordinal-one inventory record]
    ISTREAM --> ICOLLECT[Collect the initial state and record for this enabled stream]
    IRECORD --> ICOLLECT
    ICOLLECT --> IMORE{Another enabled stream requires initialization}
    IMORE -- Yes --> SEGID
    IMORE -- No --> ISINK[BuildInitialFeatureLogSinkStateAction from all enabled streams]
    EXISTS -- Every enabled stream has segments --> RECOVER[Run RecoverFeatureLogTailAction for every enabled stream<br/>validate pipe-delimited heading/control/data rows and truncate only<br/>an incomplete final event or prompt row]
    EXISTS -- Mixed, raced or invalid startup set --> SFAILREL
    ISINK --> INVENTORY[Build and validate segment inventory and sink state]
    RECOVER --> RSINK[BuildRecoveredFeatureLogSinkStateAction<br/>assemble all recovered stream states and records without touching segments]
    RSINK --> INVENTORY
    INVENTORY --> RETAIN[BuildFeatureLogRetentionAuthorizationAction<br/>select only eligible closed segments under each matching held capability]
    RETAIN --> PRUNE[PruneFeatureLogSegmentAction<br/>delete only explicitly authorized closed segments under that capability]
    PRUNE --> SRELEASE[ReleaseFeatureLogStreamLockAction once per held startup capability<br/>in deterministic stream order; attempt every terminal release and collect outcomes]
    SRELEASE -- Every capability released --> READY[Feature log sink ready; no startup lock remains held]
    SRELEASE -- Any release failure after all other releases attempted --> FAULT
    SFAILREL[ReleaseFeatureLogStreamLockAction once for every already validated<br/>startup capability with an error/cancel outcome; acquire no new lock] --> FAULT
    INSPECT -- Failure --> SFAILREL
    SEGID -- Failure --> SFAILREL
    ISTREAM -- Failure --> SFAILREL
    IRECORD -- Failure --> SFAILREL
    ISINK -- Failure --> SFAILREL
    RSINK -- Failure --> SFAILREL

    REFRESH[Any committed successor bootstrap whose validated change plan requires<br/>transitionFeatureLogging; pause normal workflow nodes and buffer only bounded<br/>workflow-attributed WorkflowTelemetryFacts] --> NPOLICY[BuildFeatureLogPolicyIdAction, BuildFeatureLogPolicyAction and<br/>ValidateFeatureLogPolicyAction for the committed successor;<br/>BuildFeatureLogBindingIdAction, ResolveFeatureLogBindingAction and<br/>ValidateFeatureLogBindingAction for the same feature/run]
    NPOLICY --> TBUILD[BuildFeatureLogPolicyTransitionAction then<br/>ValidateFeatureLogPolicyTransitionAction with current/successor authorities,<br/>materialized change evidence, policies, bindings and complete enabled-stream set]
    TBUILD --> TNEXT{Next enabled stream in fixed event then prompt order}
    TNEXT -- Yes --> TACQUIRE[AcquireFeatureLogStreamLockAction under the current binding<br/>for the exact featureId, runId and stream physical lock tuple]
    TACQUIRE -- Raw observation --> TLOCK{ValidateFeatureLogStreamLockAction<br/>produce one current-binding held capability only}
    TACQUIRE -- Contention or acquisition failure --> TFAULTREL
    TLOCK -- Invalid --> TREJECT[ReleaseRejectedFeatureLogStreamLockObservationAction]
    TREJECT --> TFAULTREL
    TLOCK -- Valid --> TWRAP[BuildFeatureLogPolicyTransitionStreamLockCapabilityAction<br/>build a nonauthorizing wrapper candidate without consuming the ordinary capability]
    TWRAP --> TDUAL{ValidateFeatureLogPolicyTransitionStreamLockCapabilityAction<br/>atomically swap/consume the ordinary capability only on success}
    TWRAP -- Build failure --> TORDREL[ReleaseFeatureLogStreamLockAction<br/>release the still-valid ordinary current-binding capability]
    TDUAL -- Rejected; ordinary capability retained --> TORDREL
    TORDREL --> FAULT
    TDUAL -- Valid dual-binding capability --> TOLDINSPECT[InspectFeatureLogStreamAction using the old side<br/>against the exact historical policy/binding]
    TOLDINSPECT -- existing-active-tail --> TOLD[RecoverFeatureLogTailAction<br/>validate pipe-delimited structure and truncate only an incomplete<br/>last event or prompt row under historical authority]
    TOLD --> TCLOSE[CloseFeatureLogStreamForPolicyTransitionAction<br/>fsync and close the old-binding active segment; create no successor]
    TOLDINSPECT -- existing-closed-only --> TCLOSED[ValidateClosedHistoricalFeatureLogStreamAction<br/>reconstruct exact close-boundary evidence without rewriting the trailer]
    TOLDINSPECT -- missing or corrupt --> TFAULTREL
    TCLOSE --> TNEW
    TCLOSED --> TNEW[InspectFeatureLogStreamAction using the successor side of the same transition capability;<br/>initialize its next nonreused segment with AssignFeatureLogSegmentIdAction,<br/>CreateInitialFeatureLogSegmentAction and initial stream/record builders,<br/>or RecoverFeatureLogTailAction if a same-process partial switch already created that tail]
    TNEW --> TVALID[ValidateFeatureLogPolicyTransitionStreamAction<br/>prove old tail closed and exactly one successor-binding active tail]
    TVALID --> TCOLLECT[Collect this stream's validated transition evidence and<br/>initialized-or-recovered successor state/inventory]
    TCOLLECT --> TRELEASE[ReleaseFeatureLogPolicyTransitionStreamLockAction<br/>release the one wrapped physical token with the terminal transition outcome]
    TRELEASE --> TNEXT
    TNEXT -- Complete --> TSINK[AssignFeatureLogSinkStateIdAction then<br/>BuildTransitionSuccessorFeatureLogSinkStateAction and<br/>ValidateTransitionSuccessorFeatureLogSinkStateAction over the complete mixed<br/>initialized/recovered successor stream set and transition evidence]
    TSINK --> TACTIVATE[ActivateFeatureLogPolicyTransitionAction<br/>atomically swap the run-local observer only after every stream is safe]
    TACTIVATE --> READY
    TOLD -- Failure --> TFAULTREL[ReleaseFeatureLogPolicyTransitionStreamLockAction for every validated<br/>dual-binding transition capability with a typed failure outcome]
    TOLDINSPECT -- Failure --> TFAULTREL
    TCLOSED -- Failure --> TFAULTREL
    TCLOSE -- Failure --> TFAULTREL
    TNEW -- Failure --> TFAULTREL
    TVALID -- Failure --> TFAULTREL
    TSINK -- Failure --> FAULT
    TRELEASE -- Failure --> FAULT
    TFAULTREL --> FAULT

    WLOG[Calling workflow owns WorkflowLog<br/>validates one four-character shortcode;<br/>log appends WorkflowTelemetryFact only] --> RUNNER
    RUNNER[PipelineRunner] -- workflow-attributed trusted lifecycle --> OBS[PipelineTelemetryObserver]
    RUNNER -- contract-accepted WorkflowTelemetryFacts from applied NodeDelta --> OBS
    WLOG --> DRAFT
    OBS --> LROOT[Runner-owned instrumentation root binding]
    LROOT --> LOG[FeatureLoggingOrchestrator<br/>coordination only; no logger in NodeRuntime]
    READY --> LOG
    LOG -- Failure before a validated stream lock exists --> FAULT

    LOG --> RESOLVE[ResolveLogEventDefinitionAction]
    RESOLVE --> DRAFT[BuildLogEventDraftAction<br/>project allowed IDs, enums, counts, timings and outcomes only]
    DRAFT --> REDACT[RedactLogFieldAction for each classified field<br/>omit secrets and arbitrary/raw content]
    REDACT --> THRESHOLD[EvaluateLogThresholdAction<br/>emit exactly when event rank is at least configured rank]
    THRESHOLD -- Below threshold --> DROP[Drop draft without allocating event ID, sequence or stream lock]
    DROP --> DDROP[DestroyRawPromptLogHandlesAction]
    DDROP --> NEXT

    THRESHOLD -- Emit --> SEQ[AssignLogEventSequenceAction<br/>trusted timestamp, event ID and next per-run/per-stream sequence]
    SEQ --> PROMPT{Sanitized prompt fragment set supplied}
    PROMPT -- No --> SAFE[ValidateSafeLogRecordAction]
    PROMPT -- Yes --> PENABLED{Prompt logging explicitly enabled}
    PENABLED -- Yes --> SAN[Redact mandatory patterns and secrets; truncate each bounded fragment]
    SAN --> PVALID[Sort by promptBodyFragmentId and validate each sanitized fragment;<br/>expand to one scalar-only prompt row per fragment;<br/>no metadata, evidence-vector or composite cells]
    PVALID -- Valid --> SAFE
    PVALID -- Invalid --> FAULT
    PENABLED -- No --> OMIT[Omit exchange; retain metadata-only event]
    OMIT --> SAFE
    SAFE -- Invalid or oversized --> FAULT[Logging safety or sink failure]
    DELIMITEDSCHEMA --> SAFE
    SAFE -- Valid --> SERIAL[SerializeFeatureLogRecordAction<br/>one event row or one row per sanitized prompt fragment<br/>in the exact built-in stream column order plus LF;<br/>no repeated or configurable heading]
    SERIAL --> EDESTROY[DestroyRawPromptLogHandlesAction<br/>safe serialized pipe-delimited row remains; transient fragments do not]
    EDESTROY --> EACQUIRE[AcquireFeatureLogStreamLockAction<br/>only after the complete bounded pipe-delimited data row is encoded;<br/>one attempt, fixed 2000 ms deadline, no backoff;<br/>lock the row's exact featureId, runId and stream tuple]
    EACQUIRE -- Contention or acquisition failure --> FAULT
    EACQUIRE -- Raw observation --> ELOCK{ValidateFeatureLogStreamLockAction<br/>exact owner, binding, adapter and runner lock-table uniqueness}
    ELOCK -- Invalid --> EREJECT[ReleaseRejectedFeatureLogStreamLockObservationAction<br/>terminalize the rejected raw acquired-lock observation]
    EREJECT --> FAULT
    ELOCK -- Valid --> RNEED[EvaluateFeatureLogRotationNeedAction<br/>check active capacity and hard lifetime maxSegments<br/>under the exact matching held capability]
    RNEED --> RDEC{Rotation-need result}
    RDEC -- Append current --> APPEND
    RDEC -- LOG_SEGMENT_LIMIT_EXHAUSTED --> EXHAUST[Retention cannot reclaim or reuse<br/>an active-run ordinal]
    EXHAUST --> EFAILREL
    RDEC -- Rotation required with exact next ordinal --> NSEG[AssignFeatureLogSegmentIdAction for the exact next ordinal]
    NSEG --> RAUTH[BuildLogRotationAuthorizationAction<br/>bind request, next identity and current sink revision without redeciding fit]
    RAUTH --> RSEG[RotateFeatureLogSegmentAction<br/>flush and close active segment; exclusive-create authorized next ordinal]
    RSEG --> RRETAIN[BuildFeatureLogRetentionAuthorizationAction<br/>after rotation closes with segment_trailer and creates the next<br/>pipe-delimited heading plus segment_header rows, select eligible closed segments only]
    RRETAIN --> RPRUNE[PruneFeatureLogSegmentAction<br/>delete only the single-use authorized closed set under the held lock]
    RPRUNE --> APPEND[AppendFeatureLogRecordAction<br/>append one complete pipe-delimited data row with expected sequence/segment state,<br/>apply mandatory flush policy and advance sink state]
    APPEND -- Success --> ERELEASE[ReleaseFeatureLogStreamLockAction<br/>release this exact capability with the successful append outcome]
    ERELEASE -- Released --> NEXT[Continue workflow; no stream lock remains held;<br/>logs remain outside stage/task transaction membership]
    ERELEASE -- Release failure --> FAULT
    EFAILREL[ReleaseFeatureLogStreamLockAction<br/>release the exact held append capability with its error/cancel outcome] --> FAULT

    CREATE -- Failure --> SFAILREL
    RECOVER -- Interior corruption or recovery failure --> SFAILREL
    INVENTORY -- Invalid --> SFAILREL
    RETAIN -- Failure --> SFAILREL
    PRUNE -- Failure --> SFAILREL
    RNEED -- Invalid rotation result --> EFAILREL
    NSEG -- Failure --> EFAILREL
    RAUTH -- Failure --> EFAILREL
    RSEG -- Failure --> EFAILREL
    RRETAIN -- Failure --> EFAILREL
    RPRUNE -- Failure --> EFAILREL
    APPEND -- Failure --> EFAILREL
    FAULT --> FDESTROY[DestroyRawPromptLogHandlesAction if transient handles remain]
    FDESTROY --> EMERGENCY[EmitEmergencyLogFailureRecordAction<br/>one direct stderr attempt, max 128 ASCII bytes:<br/>SDDE_LOG_FAILURE workflow=CODE level=fatal code=FAILURE_CODE]
    EMERGENCY --> TXSTATE{Workflow, stage or task transaction is prepared or applying}
    TXSTATE -- No --> STABLE[Typed no-prepared-transaction stable-boundary outcome]
    TXSTATE -- Yes --> RECOVERY[Invoke the recovery subroutine in diagram 09:<br/>acquire the exact project/feature collection lock, validate storage capability,<br/>run TransactionRecoveryOrchestrator and ReadTransactionRecoveryStateAction;<br/>RestoreTransactionEntryAction in reverse without a marker or<br/>VerifyCommittedTransactionEntryAction forward with a marker;<br/>commit/retire transaction ID, clean up and release exactly once]
    RECOVERY --> STABLE
    STABLE --> BLOCK[BuildLoggingBlockedControlAction<br/>block the runner before its next node]

    LOG -. compiler-locked logging action IDs are excluded from observation .-> OBS
